EXACT INDEX ALIGNMENT (find the shift that makes them coincide)
======================================================================
d=3
strip length L : tilings = a_d(L)
indep sets of P_v^{d-1} as function of v:
  v=0: indep=1  matches a_d(L) for L in [0, 1, 2]
  v=1: indep=2  matches a_d(L) for L in [3]
  v=2: indep=3  matches a_d(L) for L in [4]
  v=3: indep=4  matches a_d(L) for L in [5]
  v=4: indep=6  matches a_d(L) for L in [6]
  v=5: indep=9  matches a_d(L) for L in [7]
  v=6: indep=13  matches a_d(L) for L in [8]
  v=7: indep=19  matches a_d(L) for L in [9]
  v=8: indep=28  matches a_d(L) for L in [10]

binary strings gap>=d of length L (consecutive 1s >= d apart):
  L=0: count=1  matches a_d(LL) for LL in [0, 1, 2]
  L=1: count=2  matches a_d(LL) for LL in [3]
  L=2: count=3  matches a_d(LL) for LL in [4]
  L=3: count=4  matches a_d(LL) for LL in [5]
  L=4: count=6  matches a_d(LL) for LL in [6]
